From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: tetris: stop ignoring unused clocks

The bring-up DT forces clk_ignore_unused on every boot. That prevents the
clock framework from disabling clocks without active consumers and masks
missing clock ownership, while also making a low-power idle baseline
impossible.

Drop the temporary command-line option now that the stable image has
working USB NCM, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, audio, charging and thermal telemetry.
Keep this as a separate patch so the first CI image can be cold-booted with
the existing image as rollback and every established subsystem can be
regression-tested.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts
@@ -19,9 +19,7 @@
 		serial0 = &uart0;
 	};
 
-	// NOTE: Will be replaced by our to-be-bootloader. Keep in for now.
 	chosen {
-		bootargs = "clk_ignore_unused";
 		#address-cells = <2>;
 		#size-cells = <2>;
 		ranges;
-- 
